D) Historical relics that have disappeared can be restored through reconstruction.
The context actually argues against this idea. It suggests that while technically buildings can be rebuilt, the history and culture they carry are difficult to reproduce. Therefore, this option contradicts the main message of the text.

Based on the analysis, the option that best captures the main point of the text is:

A) Protecting cultural relics requires awe and respect for the history and culture behind them.

