The context states that an important sign of modern industrial civilization replacing traditional agricultural civilization is the shift from traditional small-scale production and natural economy to socialized large-scale production. This shift involves not just a change in the mode of production but also a change in the cultural mode. The context further explains that socialized large-scale production operates based on rational and scientific principles provided by the cultural model of rationalism and modern organizational principles that embody the rational spirit.

