This option is about the advancement of computer technology. The argument doesn't make any claims about the future development of computer technology. It's based on the premise that computers can never have emotions, not on the limitation of technological advancement. Therefore, this option is not the correct assumption.

C) A computer could have emotions only if it could display intelligence.
