This option suggests that most of the successful donations came from new donors. If this is true, it would contradict the argument that the fundraisers are only contacting likely donors (i.e., past donors). Instead, it would imply that the fundraisers are successfully reaching out to new, potentially less likely prospects. Therefore, this option weakens the argument that the high success rate indicates insufficient canvassing effort.

