D) The $500,000 cost figure for the additional training of ground crews includes the wages that those crews will earn during the time spent in actual training.
- This option provides information about the cost structure of the training but doesn't explain why the repair costs would drop by more than half.

The option that best explains why the drop in repair costs can be expected to be much greater than the reduction in the number of collisions is Option C. If the training focuses on avoiding the most costly collisions, then even if the total number of collisions is only reduced by about half, the reduction in repair costs could be significantly greater because the most expensive collisions are being prevented.

Therefore, the correct answer is:

C) The additional training will focus on helping ground crews avoid those kinds of ground collisions that cause the most costly damage. 51%|█████     | 305/600 [1:15:41<1:02:55, 12.80s/it] 51%|█████     | 306/600 [1:15:50<57:07, 11.66s/it]   51%|█████     | 307/600 [1:16:03<58:02, 11.88s/it]
