The printing and dyeing factory should pay Aetna trading company 1.56 million yuan (20% of the contract amount) as a good faith deposit to perform the contract. However, the factory paid only 1 million yuan because of financial constraints. Here, the payment is explicitly described as a good faith deposit to perform the contract, which matches the definition of a deposit.

Now let's compare the options that seem to fit the definition of a deposit:

