5. Overall, adopting the new process will cost much but bring no profit to the company.

The Supervisor agrees with the Plant Manager's overall conclusion that adopting the new process will not bring profit to the company but disagrees with one point made by the Plant Manager. The Supervisor states, "I agree with your overall conclusion, but disagree about one point you make, since the latest closed furnaces are extremely fuel-efficient."

The Supervisor's statement about the latest closed furnaces being extremely fuel-efficient suggests that they disagree with the Plant Manager's point related to the cost or efficiency of the closed furnaces.

Now let's evaluate the options:

A) Whether the new copper-smelting process releases less sulfur dioxide gas into the atmosphere than the current process.
