- Option A suggests that the placebo effect is due to multiple factors. This doesn't necessarily contradict the role of expectations; it just says there are other factors involved as well.
- Option B supports the explanation by stating that Alzheimer's patients, who can't anticipate the future, don't experience the placebo effect.
