**Option D:** Xiao Li, Xiao Wang, and Xiao Liu who have just been recruited by the company live in a temporary warehouse of the company.

This option describes three individuals (Xiao Li, Xiao Wang, and Xiao Liu) who have just been recruited by a company and are living in a temporary warehouse. This suggests that they might be facing financial constraints and possibly cannot afford commercial housing. They likely do not have enough money to buy a house and might not qualify for certain government housing programs due to their financial situation or other eligibility criteria.

Based on the context provided for the sandwich layer, Option D fits the description best. These individuals seem to be in a situation where they might not have the means to buy affordable or commercial houses and may fall into the category of people who are caught between different housing options and financial constraints.

